You’re basically building a dynamic evaluation form per Section in Power Apps, then sharing the link so the Section In-Charge can answer. This is very doable—and your UI idea is good 👍

Let me guide you with a clear design + working approach.


---

🧩 1. Data Structure (IMPORTANT)

Use these SharePoint lists (as mentioned earlier):

Sections

Suppliers

Questions

Evaluations (answers)


👉 The key is:
Each answer = 1 record per Supplier + Question


---

🎯 2. Your Target UI (Matrix Type)

You want something like:

Section: PR PROC

Supplier | Code   | M1R | M5R | D3R
-----------------------------------
AOI      | 343434 |  1  |  2  |  3
ASIA     | 456789 |  2  |  1  |  3

👉 This is called a matrix/grid form


---

⚙️ 3. Build in Power Apps

Step 1: Section Selection (or from link)

Add Dropdown:

Dropdown_Section
Items = Sections


---

Step 2: Pass Section via Link 🔗

When sending form:

https://apps.powerapps.com/play/...&section=PR PROC

Then in App:

Set(varSection, Param("section"))

Set default:

Dropdown_Section.Default = varSection

👉 Now when user opens link → Section auto selected ✅


---

Step 3: Show Suppliers per Section

Insert Gallery (Vertical)

Gallery_Suppliers.Items =
Filter(Suppliers, Section.Value = Dropdown_Section.Selected.Title)

Inside gallery show:

Supplier Name

Supplier Code



---

Step 4: Show Questions as Columns (M1R, M5R)

Since Power Apps doesn’t support true tables easily, do this:

👉 Inside each supplier row, manually create columns:

Example:

Label	Radio Button

M1R	Radio_M1R
M5R	Radio_M5R



---

Step 5: Add Score Selection (1,2,3)

For each question:

Radio_M1R.Items = [1,2,3]
Radio_M5R.Items = [1,2,3]


---

💾 Step 6: Save Data (Important)

Add Submit Button

OnSelect:

ForAll(
    Gallery_Suppliers.AllItems,
    
    Patch(Evaluations, Defaults(Evaluations),
    {
        Section: Dropdown_Section.Selected,
        Supplier: ThisRecord.SupplierName,
        
        Question: "M1R",
        Score: Radio_M1R.Selected.Value
    });

    Patch(Evaluations, Defaults(Evaluations),
    {
        Section: Dropdown_Section.Selected,
        Supplier: ThisRecord.SupplierName,
        
        Question: "M5R",
        Score: Radio_M5R.Selected.Value
    })
)

👉 This saves:

AOI + M1R + Score

AOI + M5R + Score



---

🔥 4. Better (Dynamic Questions per Section)

Instead of hardcoding M1R, M5R:

Use a nested gallery

Outer Gallery → Suppliers

Inner Gallery → Questions

Inner gallery:

Filter(Questions, Section.Value = Dropdown_Section.Selected.Title)

Inside:

Question label (M1R)

Radio (1,2,3)



---

🔗 5. Sending the Link

Example:

https://apps.powerapps.com/play/APPID?section=PR PROC

Send to:

Section In-Charge


👉 They open → auto filtered → answer only their section


---

🧠 6. Key Tips (VERY IMPORTANT)

✔ Use Lookup columns properly in SharePoint
✔ Use Param() for dynamic link
✔ Use ForAll + Patch for saving
✔ Avoid hardcoding if many questions


